Proposed patch for hpe-networking-mcp. Casper does not apply it.

Adds one router-level tool, access_check, that answers the
"casper/access-check v1" contract Casper reads (src/mcp/access.ts):

  {"contract": "casper/access-check v1",
   "products": [{"product", "access": "read-only"|"read-write"|"unknown",
                 "identity", "role", "server_gate": {"env_var", "state"}}]}

- Always on (like catalog-core), annotations=READ_ONLY, no arguments.
- Reports only the platforms whose backend is loaded.
- Mist: GET /api/v1/self. Read-only only if every privilege role is "read"
  ("helpdesk" counts as read-write until someone confirms what it can do).
- ClearPass: GET /api/oauth/me and GET /api/oauth/privileges. Read-only only
  if every privilege is a read-only ('#'-prefixed) one.
- Central/GLP: role assignments for the token's principal, then each role's
  permissions. Paths and the principal format are marked CONFIRM and must be
  checked against vendor/openapi/glp before merging.
- Every product also reports platform_write_gate_state() as server_gate, so a
  client can confirm that its read-only settings took hold.
- Never returns tokens. Any error or odd payload gives "unknown".

Casper also reads "casper/access-check v2": the same answer, plus per product
"can_change" and "read_only" lists of {"kind": "org"|"site"|"sitegroup",
"id", "name"} saying where the login can change things. The server enforces
those lists; Casper only shows them. This patch still answers v1.

The read-only settings need no change here: Casper sets
HPE_MCP_ACCESS_PROFILE, HPE_MCP_READONLY, HPE_MCP_PRODUCT_ACCESS and every
HPE_MCP_*_WRITES from outside, and load_dotenv(override=False) keeps them.

Apply from the hpe-networking-mcp repository root:
  git apply hpe-networking-mcp-access-check.patch

